; map-representation group-choice arms with fixed keys OUTSIDE the supported uint/text kinds.
; Key writing/verification (and `{name}_key_encoding` under --preserve-encodings) is only
; implemented for uint and text keys — parity with the record map path, which panics on other key
; kinds (`unsupported map key type`, ledgered in cddl-matrix/ROADMAP.md § findings). The
; group-choice collapse rejects them gracefully UP FRONT instead of reaching that panic; flipping
; either rule to `ok` means real nint/float key support landed (do the record path first).
neg = { -1: uint // b: tstr }
flt = { 1.5: uint // b: tstr }
